first have the application and docker file and build images
in mini kube this image wont be there when we run the deployment it pull image from minikube docker engine so it will search there
so do minikube image load <image_name> to load the image in minikube docker engine


Create deployment.yaml:

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: python-deployment
  labels: 
    app: dev
spec:
  replicas: 2 

  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: dev
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: dev
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: python-kube
        image: test:v1
        ports:
        - containerPort: 8000

run the command to create deployment:
kubectl create -f deployment.yaml

to see the pod details:
kubectl get pods
kubectl get pods -o wide 
kubectl get pods -v=7 or -v=9 to see the details of the pod how it is created and what is the process of creating the pod.


Now create service.yaml to expose the deployment (node port service) to the external world:
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: python-service
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    app: dev
  ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 8080
      targetPort: 8000
      nodePort: 30080
